Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: rearm station TXQs after successful link changes

mac80211 publishes the new valid-link mask before change_sta_links(). A TX
worker can then leave a shared TXQ unscheduled while the old sleeping
primary still owns it. After promotion to an awake link, an awake frame's
completion need not rearm that TXQ because neither WCID is in power save.

Rearm the station's TXQs once the successful MLO change has selected a
published active primary. This does not change per-link PS flags or the
completion hot path. Do not rearm failed changes: mac80211 restores its
valid-link mask after the callback returns, so that rollback boundary
requires separate handling. No sleep/wake hardware fix is claimed here.

---
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1483,10 +1483,11 @@
 			    struct ieee80211_sta *sta, u16 old_links,
 			    u16 new_links)
 {
+	struct mt7996_sta *msta = (struct mt7996_sta *)sta->drv_priv;
 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = mt7996_hw_dev(hw);
 	unsigned long add = new_links & ~old_links;
 	unsigned long rem = old_links & ~new_links;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, i;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
@@ -1493,6 +1494,24 @@
 	mt7996_mac_sta_remove_links(dev, vif, sta, rem, false);
 	ret = mt7996_mac_sta_add_links(dev, vif, sta, add);
 
+	if (!ret && sta->mlo &&
+	    msta->deflink_id < IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS &&
+	    (new_links & BIT(msta->deflink_id))) {
+		struct mt7996_sta_link *link;
+
+		link = mt76_dereference(msta->link[msta->deflink_id], &dev->mt76);
+		if (link && link->wcid.link_valid) {
+			/*
+			 * A TXQ gated by the old primary may have left the
+			 * airtime scheduler before the link selectors changed.
+			 */
+			for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sta->txq); i++)
+				if (sta->txq[i])
+					ieee80211_schedule_txq(hw, sta->txq[i]);
+			mt76_worker_schedule(&dev->mt76.tx_worker);
+		}
+	}
+
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
 	return ret;
